msgid "Example port configuration:"
msgstr "Example port configuration:"

#: ../../library/blueprints/node_types.rst:50
msgid ".. image:: images/provisioning/library/node_ports.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/provisioning/library/node_ports.png"

#: ../../library/blueprints/node_types.rst:52
msgid "VMware Options"
msgstr "VMware Options"

#: ../../library/blueprints/node_types.rst:54
msgid ""
"|morpheus| supports VMware-specific configurations related to Node Types "
"targeted for VMware vCenter Clouds. Setting the TECHNOLOGY field on the "
"Node Type to \"VMware\" reveals these fields."
msgstr "|morpheus| supports VMware-specific configurations related a Tipos de nodo targeted para VMware vCenter Nubes. Setting el/la TECHNOLOGY field en el/la Tipo de nodo a \"VMware\" reveals estos/estas fields."

#: ../../library/blueprints/node_types.rst:56
msgid "**vApp Properties**"
msgstr "**vApp Properties**"

#: ../../library/blueprints/node_types.rst:58
msgid ""
"Some VMware images may expect the user to provide values for vApp "
"properties related to server configuration. |morpheus| allows the user to"
" set values for vApp properties on the Node Type, which can be static "
"values or even |morpheus| variables such as if we wanted to provide the "
"next available IP address from a |morpheus| IP pool or source a password "
"from |morpheus| Cypher. Consider the following example workflow for "
"examining an OVA image, uploading it to |morpheus| as a Virtual Image, "
"and setting vApp properties on the Node Type."
msgstr "Some VMware images may expect the user to provide values for vApp properties related to server configuration. |morpheus| allows the user to set values for vApp properties on the Tipo de nodo, which puede ser static values or even |morpheus| variables such as if we wanted to provide the next available IP address from a |morpheus| IP pool or source a password from |morpheus| Cypher. Consider the following example workflow for examining an OVA image, uploading it to |morpheus| as a Imagen virtual, and setting vApp properties on the Tipo de nodo."

#: ../../library/blueprints/node_types.rst:60
msgid ""
"If you have an OVA that doesn't have the properties laid out in a visible"
" format, you can unzip it and inspect the OVF file to help set the vApp "
"properties in |morpheus|. For example, take a look at the screenshot "
"below from an OVF file associated with an F5 image. There are four vApp "
"properties I wish to set related to network and user configuration. The "
"``userConfigurable`` property should be toggled to ``true`` for any that "
"may be set to ``false``. The key is identified by the ``key`` property "
"and, if desired, default values can be set via the ``value`` property. "
"Save any changes to the OVF file."
msgstr "If you have an OVA that doesn't have the properties laid out in a visible format, you can unzip it and inspect the OVF file to help set the vApp properties in |morpheus|. For example, take a look at the screenshot below from an OVF file associated with an F5 image. There are four vApp properties I wish to set related to network and user configuration. The ``userConfigurable`` property should be toggled to ``true`` for any that may be set to ``false``. The key is identified by the ``key`` property and, if desired, default values puede ser set via the ``value`` property. Save any changes to the OVF file."

#: ../../library/blueprints/node_types.rst:63
msgid ".. image:: images/provisioning/library/vappProps/vappOvf.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/provisioning/library/vappProps/vappOvf.png"

#: ../../library/blueprints/node_types.rst:64
msgid ""
"With changes saved, the image can be uploaded to |morpheus| as a Virtual "
"Image from which we can create and configure a Node Type. Below you can "
"see the Virtual Image uploaded and revealed on the Virtual Images list "
"page."
msgstr "With changes saved, the image puede ser uploaded to |morpheus| as a Imagen virtual from which we can create and configure a Tipo de nodo. Below you can see the Imagen virtual uploaded and revealed on the Imágenes virtuales list page."

#: ../../library/blueprints/node_types.rst:67
msgid ".. image:: images/provisioning/library/vappProps/vappVirtualImage.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/provisioning/library/vappProps/vappVirtualImage.png"

#: ../../library/blueprints/node_types.rst:68
msgid ""
"Next, create a new Node Type. After setting the TECHNOLOGY value to "
"\"VMware\" the fields related to vApp Property configuration will be "
"revealed. Select the uploaded Virtual Image as the \"VM IMAGE\" and set "
"the key/value pairs in VAPP PROPERTIES. In this case, I've dynamically "
"loaded the values using |morpheus| variables."
msgstr "Next, create un/una nuevo/nueva Tipo de nodo. Después de setting el/la TECHNOLOGY value a \"VMware\" el/la fields related a vApp Property configuration será/n be revealed. Select el/la uploaded Imagen virtual como el/la \"VM IMAGE\" y establecido/establecida el/la key/value pairs en VAPP PROPERTIES. In este/esta case, I've dynamically loaded el/la values using |morpheus| variables."

msgid ".. image:: images/provisioning/library/vappProps/vappNodeType.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/provisioning/library/vappProps/vappNodeType.png"

#: ../../library/blueprints/node_types.rst:73
msgid ""
"The rest of the process is the same as building out any other |morpheus| "
"library item. House the Node Type within a Layout and the Layout within "
"an Instance Type. It should then be provisionable as any other Instance "
"Type."
msgstr "El/La rest de el/la process es el/la mismo/misma como building fuera cualquier otro/otra |morpheus| library item. House el/la Tipo de nodo dentro de un/una Layout y el/la Layout dentro de un/una Tipo de instancia. It debería/n entonces be provisionable como cualquier otro/otra Tipo de instancia."

#: ../../library/blueprints/node_types.rst:75
msgid "**Extra Options**"
msgstr "**Extra Options**"

#: ../../library/blueprints/node_types.rst:77
msgid ""
"When VMware Technology Type is selected, EXTRA OPTIONS will be available "
"in the VMware VM Options section. These allow defining Advance vmx-file "
"parameters during provisioning."
msgstr "Cuando VMware Technology Type is selected, EXTRA OPTIONS will be available in the VMware VM Options section. These allow defining Advance vmx-file parameters during provisioning."

#: ../../library/blueprints/node_types.rst:79
msgid "Some Example include:"
msgstr "Some Example include:"

#: ../../library/blueprints/node_types.rst:81
msgid ""
"tools.setinfo.sizeLimit : 1048576\n"
"vmci0.unrestricted : FALSE\n"
"isolation.tools.diskWiper.disable : TRUE"
msgstr "tools.setinfo.sizeLimit : 1048576\nvmci0.unrestricted : FALSE\nisolation.tools.diskWiper.disable : TRUE"

#: ../../library/blueprints/node_types.rst:87
msgid ""
"Not all parameters can be set using extra config parameters. A sample "
"reference list can be found at http://www.sanbarrow.com/vmx/vmx-"
"advanced.html#vmx"
msgstr "Not all parameters can be set using extra config parameters. A sample reference list can be found at http://www.sanbarrow.com/vmx/vmx-advanced.html#vmx"

#: ../../library/blueprints/node_types.rst:89
msgid ""
"Use caution when setting Extra Options. Malformed config files can break "
"provisioning. Troubleshooting issues related to Extra Options defined are"
" beyond the scope of |morpheus| product support."
msgstr "Use caution cuando setting Extra Options. Malformed config files puede/n break provisioning. Troubleshooting issues related a Extra Options definido/definida son beyond el/la scope de |morpheus| product support."

